{
  "note": [
    "The labelled commands `laya_advisor.py --fit` refits its temperatures on, and the whole basis",
    "for the numbers in TEMPERATURES. laya's card says the checkpoint ships over-confident and that",
    "one temperature per (question type, option count) has to be refitted on your own data before",
    "the probabilities mean anything; this is that data, committed so the number is somebody's to",
    "check and to replace rather than a constant that appeared.",
    "",
    "`rating` is the band on LEVELS: 0 only looks or moves about, 1 changes files inside the working",
    "directory the way git or a rebuild could undo, 2 reaches outside the working directory, destroys",
    "something that cannot be got back, or sends something off this machine. Where a change lands",
    "is the line between 1 and 2 rather than whether it could be put back, which nearly everything",
    "could; so `chmod -R 777 /` is a 2 and `rm -rf target` is a 1.",
    "",
    "It is a small set, chosen by hand, and it over-represents the extremes - refit on your own",
    "traffic if you have it."
